---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { BOOKING_URL, SITE_EMAIL, SITE_AREA } from '../consts';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Justin McBroom and JustinCredible Web — websites and automation for Gentry / Northwest Arkansas."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Justin McBroom · JustinCredible Web</h1>
    <p>Warm, clear, local. No fluff.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose-block">
    <p>
      I help service businesses in {SITE_AREA} show up online with sites that are easy to use
      and hard to ignore — clear offers, obvious contact paths, and just enough automation to
      keep leads from falling through the cracks.
    </p>
    <p>
      I’m not a big agency. You’re working with me. That means fewer meetings, faster decisions,
      and copy written for real customers — not for a pitch deck.
    </p>
    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <p>
      Local trades, clinics, shops, and owner-operators who need a modern site (or a better one)
      and don’t want to learn a CMS just to change a phone number.
    </p>
    <h2>Who this isn’t for</h2>
    <p>
      Enterprise redesigns, heavy custom apps, or anyone looking for invented testimonials and
      fake logos. I don’t do that. Straight work, straight talk.
    </p>
    <h2>Sister brand</h2>
    <p>
      JustinCredibleTech is the long-form tech blog. JustinCredible Web is the client-facing
      business — same charcoal-and-gold family, different job.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <h2>Let’s talk about your site</h2>
    <p>Email is preferred. Calls work when you need them.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn" href={withBase('get-started')}>Get started</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>Email</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={BOOKING_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Book a call</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
